# size: 1200x820
# The detail editors switch on the edited task's own lifetime, so two tasks in
# one column never share native input lifetimes. This scenario guards the fix
# for the defect where selecting a second equal-valued task in the same column
# retained the first task's editor, and with it an undo history an ordinary
# Ctrl+Z then pasted into the wrong task. Native history depth is the
# observation neither the semantic specs nor a first-frame screenshot can make.
click #edit-task-2
wait 400
focus "Task notes"
key ctrl-a
key backspace
wait 600
expect-value "Task notes"
click #edit-task-1
wait 400
focus "Task notes"
key ctrl-a
key backspace
wait 600
type "Task notes" private
wait 600
key ctrl-a
key backspace
wait 600
expect-value "Task notes"
click #edit-task-2
wait 600
expect-value "Task notes"
expect-history "Task notes" 0
